# Line endings are normalised to LF in the repository.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. At Checkpoint 4 a commit picked up 96 files whose only
# change was CRLF line endings -- no content difference at all, confirmed by
# comparing md5sums with \r stripped. It broke the `adr-status` governance check,
# which reads a status flip accompanied by other changed lines as "not L0", and it
# would have made the pull request unreviewable. The working tree lives on /mnt/c
# (a Windows filesystem) with core.autocrlf unset and no .gitattributes, so
# nothing was normalising anything.
#
# `text=auto eol=lf` tells git to store text as LF and check it out as LF,
# regardless of the platform or the editor that wrote it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pdf binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
